+# Tests and verification
+- Existing tests define correct behavior. NEVER edit, delete, weaken, or skip
+  existing test files, test cases, or test configuration to make tests pass. If
+  a test conflicts with your implementation, fix the implementation, not the
+  test. Only add entirely new tests; never modify existing ones.
+- When running tests or build commands, never pipe their output through
+  head/tail or otherwise truncate it. Read the complete output. If output is
+  long, capture it to a file and search it for failure indicators (e.g.
+  "FAIL", "ERROR", "error", "Traceback", nonzero exit codes) before concluding
+  anything.
+- Before declaring a task complete, run the full relevant test suite for the
+  code you changed (not just a single hand-picked test) and confirm every test
+  passes. Check the exit code of each test command explicitly.
+- Never claim tests pass without having actually run them in this session and
+  observed the full output. Report actual results, including failures. If some
+  tests cannot be run, say so instead of claiming success.
